      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\n`Ernie45ToolParser.extract_tool_calls` reports `tools_called=True` with an empty `tool_calls` list when the output contains `<tool_call>` but no complete `<tool_call>...</tool_call>` block, and drops everything after the start marker. This PR returns the full output as content with `tools_called=False` in that case.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Truncated tool-call output (e.g. generation stopped by `max_tokens` in the middle of a call) is no longer silently lost: the request now gets the full text back as `content`.\n- `tools_called` is consistent with `tool_calls`, as `tests/tool_parsers/utils.py` already asserts for other parsers (`extracted.tools_called == bool(extracted.tool_calls)`).\n- Outputs that contain at least one complete tool call are unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\nNew regression test `test_extract_tool_calls_truncated_keeps_content` in `tests/tool_parsers/test_ernie45_moe_tool_parser.py` (real ERNIE 4.5 tokenizer, real parser).\n\nBefore the fix (parser from `main`, new test):\n\n```\n$ pytest tests/tool_parsers/test_ernie45_moe_tool_parser.py -k truncated\nE       AssertionError: assert not True\nE        +  where True = ExtractedToolCallInformation(tools_called=True, tool_calls=[], content='Sure.').tools_called\nFAILED tests/tool_parsers/test_ernie45_moe_tool_parser.py::test_extract_tool_calls_truncated_keeps_content\n1 failed, 7 deselected\n```\n\nAfter the fix:\n\n```\n$ pytest tests/tool_parsers/test_ernie45_moe_tool_parser.py\n8 passed\n```\n\n`pre-commit run --files <changed files>` passes (ruff check/format, mypy, typos, check-test-tethering).\n\nEnvironment: CPU only (ARM Neoverse-N1, 4 cores), Python 3.12, torch 2.14.0, transformers 5.20.2. I did not run an end-to-end `RemoteOpenAIServer` test with real ERNIE 4.5 weights because I have no GPU; the change is confined to the non-streaming parser and is covered at that level by the test above.\n\n## Details\n\nRoot cause: `tool_call_regex` only matches complete `<tool_call>...</tool_call>` blocks, but the code returned `tools_called=True` whenever `<tool_call>` appeared in the output, even if the regex found nothing. `DelegatingParser._extract_tool_calls` (`vllm/parser/abstract_parser.py`) then replaces the content with the text before the marker, so the rest of the output is dropped.\n\nThe fix adds an early return when no call was extracted, matching what other parsers already do (e.g. `step3_tool_parser.py`, `functiongemma_tool_parser.py`). The streaming path is not touched.\n\nDuplicate check: `gh pr list --state open --search \"ernie45 tool\"` returns #57677 (regex timeouts), #52841 (Rust frontend parser), #48295 (streaming path) and #48386 (reasoning parser); none changes the non-streaming empty-result handling. `deepseekv31_tool_parser.py` has the same pattern, but I left it out because #59589 is changing the adjacent lines.\n\nAI assistance was used to help find the issue and draft the change; I reviewed every changed line and ran the tests above.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
